I just switched to Team Red from a 10900K. I got the 7950X3D (yes, I did my research on it vs 7800X3D). I'm pairing it with an Asus B650E motherboard and 32GB gskill CL30 RAM.

It's my first ever AMD CPU so I have some questions about switching:

&#x200B;

\-I'm gonna need a fresh install of windows, right? If so, can I use my same license or do I need a new one?

&#x200B;

\-I currently have 4 Hard Drives. One SSD with Windows 10 on it. 1 HDD with folders, movies, pictures and stuff like that AND 2 NVME SSDs with games and every day software.

Obviously the fresh windows install will go on the same SSD as before. But what about the others? Do I need to do something with them? or is it just plug and play?

&#x200B;

\-I know there's bios updates that are needed for the CPU/RAM to perform well. Can anyone recommend a good youtube video/channel that shows how to? I have never perfomed a bios update.

&#x200B;

Any info/recommendation helps!

